    "approved_definition_context": [
      "H,K with NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace over real scalars and CompleteSpace are real Hilbert spaces. E finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel includes dimension zero.",
      "A LinearPMap is a partial real-linear map with a linear-subspace domain; applying it takes a domain subtype element. Coercion of a domain element into H has the ambient H norm. IsClosed means its graph is closed in the product topology; it does not mean A is bounded or everywhere defined.",
      "IsClosable means topological closure of the graph is the graph of a partial linear map. For a closable D, D.closure has this graph. Dense domain uses the ambient L2 topology.",
      "Lp F 2 mu consists of measurable F-valued functions with finite squared-norm integral, modulo almost-everywhere equality; =ae compares representatives. The real inner product is the usual L2 inner product.",
      "ContDiff at 2/infinity means C2/smooth. HasCompactSupport means closure of nonzero support is compact. gradient is the Riesz representative of the actual Frechet derivative.",
      "Measure.tilted is normalized exponential weighting, totalized to zero if weight is not integrable. Integrable means almost-everywhere strongly measurable with finite integral of norm.",
      "Measure.map is pushforward, prod is independent product, stdGaussian is standard Gaussian. A Markov kernel is a measurably parameterized probability measure. IsCondKernel disintegrates the specified joint measure on its first coordinate; Prod.swap swaps coordinates.",
      "Lets abbreviate the displayed objects. Quantifier order follows the printed type; inverse of a positive epsilon is ordinary reciprocal."
    ]
